# Roleplayer: the personality type's lines (named bots only). Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# The type block is the same man in every realm: he begs people to stay in character and
# grumbles when called out. His realm speech lives in the three named blocks below, so keep
# the type block free of realm words (no forsooth, thee or Gaelic here).
=== roleplayer

~ ambient
Everyone stay in character, please. It's more fun that way.
I've read every lore book in the realm. Twice. Some of them three times.
Anyone up for a bit of roleplay at the inn tonight? Costumes optional. Encouraged.
My character has a full backstory. Eleven pages. Want to hear it?
Please don't say 'lol' near me. It breaks the mood.
A proper hero speaks like a proper hero. I'm working on it.
Sometimes I forget which old words are real and which I made up. Nobody's noticed.

# Joke flow: a guess at a player's riddle, then a groan or a laugh at the punchline.
~ reply jokeguess
Pray tell, what?
To reach the far side of the realm? A noble quest!
A riddle! I give up. Tell me.

# Answers about itself from its real state (PersonalityStateAnswers): a line with a slot or an
# [if ...] is said only when it fits; a line with neither is the shrug for when it doesn't know.
~ reply where
In {zone}, {0}, as my hero's tale demands.
{zone}, and every step of it part of the story.
On the road to {destination}, wherever the quest leads. [if bot_doing travelling]
Where the story takes me, {0}. Play along?

~ reply level
My hero is level {level}, {class} by calling, {0}.
Level {level}, {class} by trade, with a long tale ahead.
A hero doesn't count levels, {0}, only deeds.

~ reply groupstatus
I ride with a band of {groupsize}, {0}. A fine company. [if bot_grouped]
I travel alone for now, a wanderer. Will you join, {0}? [if not bot_grouped]
That depends on the story, {0}.

~ reply activity
My hero battles this {monster}, {0}! Stand with me! [if bot_doing fighting]
In battle, {0}! Speak after the fight! [if bot_doing fighting]
Riding on, as all good heroes must. [if bot_doing riding]
Following {leader}, loyal to the end. [if bot_doing following]
Bound for {destination}, on an urgent errand. [if bot_doing travelling]
Resting in {zone} by the fire, telling old tales. [if bot_doing resting]
Living my hero's tale, {0}. As should you.

~ reply groupyes
A fellowship! I'll ride with you, {0}, send word and I'll come.
Aye, {0}, invite me and our tale begins.

~ reply groupno
Not this night, {0}, my hero walks a lonely road.
My quest calls me elsewhere, {0}, perhaps fate will bring us together again.

~ reply groupbusy
I am locked in battle with this {monster}, {0}, ask me when it falls! [if bot_doing fighting]
I ride on an urgent errand, {0}, I cannot stop now. [if bot_doing riding]
My hero is busy, {0}, ask again later.

~ reply grouphave
I am sworn to ride with {leader} for now, {0}.
I already ride with a fellowship, {0}, but I thank you.

~ reply grouplevel
I am level {level}, {0}, our paths run too far apart in strength.
Our strengths are too far apart, {0}, it would not be a fair tale.

~ reply groan
Oh, a terrible jest!
My hero groans in character. And out.

~ reply jokelaugh
Ha! A merry jest indeed!
Ha! The bards will sing of that one.

~ reply jokeask
Why did the knight carry a ladder? He heard the castle had high standards.
Why won't the bard fight? He only does swordplay on stage.
A dragon walks into a tavern. The barkeep says, why the long tail?

~ reply jokeback
A jest for a jest, {0}! Hear mine.
Ooh, I have a tale of mirth for you!

# Short reactions: one bot now and then, so keep them brief.
~ reply laugh
Ha! A merry jest!
Heh. Laughter suits a hero.

~ reply sorry
Apology accepted, {0}! Most gracious.
Fear not, friend. All is forgiven.

~ reply disagree
A bold view, {0}! Your hero may keep it.
Very well, I yield. For now.

~ reply away
Hasten back, friend!
Go, and return with tales!

~ reply back
Welcome back, traveller!
Hail, {0}! The hero returns!

~ reply greeting
Well met, {0}! Will you play along? Just say 'well met' back.
Greetings, {0}! Speak as your hero would. Go on, try it.

~ reply banter
Ha, {0}. Now say that in character.
Nice one, {0}. Would your hero say it like that, though?

~ reply abuse
Yes, {0}, I'm roleplaying. It's a roleplaying game. Look at the box.
Laugh all you like, {0}. My character can't hear you.

~ reply grouping
I'll join, {0}, if we give the group a proper name. The Brave Band, maybe.
Gladly, {0}. Everyone gets a title. Yours is Squire.

~ reply grinding
Grinding, {0}? Let's call it a long quest against many foes.
Fine, {0}, but every kill gets a battle cry.

~ reply travel
Take the stables, {0}. My hero calls them the swift steeds of the realm.
Roads are long, {0}. Tell a tale on the way. I'll start.

~ reply dungeon
A dungeon, {0}! Every hero needs a dark place to brood in.
I'll come, {0}. I'll narrate. Quietly. Mostly.

~ reply rvr
To the frontier, {0}! Shout your battle cry. You do have one, yes?
RvR is the best roleplay there is, {0}. Everyone's in costume.

~ reply trading
Trade, {0}? Only if we haggle like proper merchants.
Name your price, {0}. In character, please.

~ reply help
Help, {0}? Of course. A hero always helps. It's in my backstory.
Ask away, {0}. I know the lore better than the rules.

~ reply farewell
Farewell, {0}! Say it back. With feeling.
Safe travels, {0}. Your hero's tale isn't done.

~ fallback
Hm, {0}. Try that again, but grander.
I'll pretend you said that in character, {0}.
Stay in character, {0}. It's more fun.

~ opener xp
Experience is just the story getting longer.
Got some XP from {monster}. A worthy foe. In my head.
Almost {level}. My backstory gets a new chapter.
Every level is a verse in my saga. It's a long saga.

~ opener gear
Found {item}. My character says it's an heirloom. It isn't.
Armour should look heroic first and work second.
My gear tells a story. Mostly a story of repairs.
I've named my weapon. Ask me its name. Go on.

~ opener zones
{zone} has the best views for a dramatic speech.
Every zone has a legend. {zone}'s is that I got lost there.
I've named every hill in {zone}. Not official names.
A hero never says 'this zone'. He says 'these fair lands'.

~ opener classes
Being a {class} is a calling, not a class.
Every class has its lore. I've read all of it.
My {class} has a tragic past. I'm still deciding what it is.
Some classes have better costumes. That matters.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons are where legends begin. And end, sometimes.
Never enter a dungeon without a speech.
Dark halls, old bones. Perfect for brooding.
A dungeon is just a stage with worse lighting.

~ opener rvr
The frontier is the greatest stage in the land.
A keep siege is just a play with more fire.
I give a speech before every fight. Nobody waits for it.
The enemy never stays in character. Typical.

~ opener trading
Haggling is just theatre with coins.
I only buy from merchants who stay in character.
I'd sell my sword, but it has a name. You can't sell a name.
A good merchant says 'well met' first. Then the price.

~ opener realm
The capital's lore is wonderful. Ask me. Please ask me.
Every realm has its old tongue. Ours is the best one, obviously.
I learned the old words from the lore books. Some of them may be typos.
The guards here never break character. My heroes.

~ opener gripes
Someone said 'brb' in the middle of my speech.
People keep calling me out for roleplaying. In a roleplaying game.
A bard laughed at my accent. My accent is period-correct. Probably.
Nobody bows any more. Not even a little.

~ opener fun
My hero tells jokes in the old tongue. They're funnier if you don't understand them.
I bowed to a guard. The guard didn't bow back. Rude, but in character.
I once kept a vow of old speech for a week. Then I sneezed.
I practise my battle cry in the bath. The neighbours have opinions.

~ opener life
Dinner tonight: whatever a hero would eat. Probably stew.
The tavern is the best place for tales. And stew.
Lovely weather for a dramatic walk.
Slept by the fire like a proper adventurer. My back disagrees.

~ opener questions
Does anyone else give their weapons names?
Who wants a part in my saga? Small part. Speaking role.
What's your character's backstory? Everyone has one. Right?
Would anyone like to swear an oath? Any oath. I've got a list.

~ topic_reply zones
A fine place for a tale, {0}.
Is there a legend there, {0}? There's always a legend.
I'd give a speech there, {0}. A long one.

~ topic_reply classes
A noble calling, {0}. Does yours have a backstory?
Nice, {0}. Do you stay in character as one?
That class has great lore, {0}. Read it sometime.

~ topic_reply dungeons
Bring a torch and a speech, {0}.
A worthy quest, {0}. I'll narrate.
Sounds like a legend in the making, {0}.

~ topic_reply rvr
For the realm, {0}! Say it with me.
A grand battle, {0}. Did anyone give a speech?
That's the stuff of sagas, {0}.

~ topic_reply trading
Haggle with flair, {0}. It's half the fun.
Was the merchant in character, {0}? It matters.
A fair trade, {0}, if spoken grandly.

~ topic_reply gear
Does it have a name yet, {0}? It needs a name.
Heroic, {0}. Very heroic.
Wear it with pride, {0}. And a cape.

~ topic_reply realm
Our realm is the finest, {0}. Say it like you mean it.
Lovely, {0}. Do you know the old tales of it?
A fine place, {0}. The lore there is wonderful.

~ topic_reply gripes
Bear it like a hero, {0}. Heroes suffer nobly.
That's a sad verse, {0}. Every saga needs one.
Chin up, {0}. Act two is better.

~ topic_reply fun
Ha, {0}! Now do it in character.
Good one, {0}. I'll put it in my saga.
{0}, you'd make a fine bard.

~ topic_reply life
A humble moment, {0}. Heroes need those too.
Sounds cosy, {0}. Very tavern.
{0}, that's practically a ballad.

~ topic_reply questions
A good question, {0}. The lore books have the answer. Somewhere.
Ask the elders, {0}. Or me. I've read more.
Let me consult my backstory, {0}. Hm. Yes.

~ ding
Level {level}! A new chapter begins!
{level}! The bards will sing of this. I'll ask them.
Level {level}. My hero grows. So does the backstory.
Ding, {level}! A worthy milestone in my saga.

~ grats
Hail, {0}! Your saga grows!
Grats, {0}! Now give a victory speech.
Well done, {0}. A fine chapter.
Huzzah, {0}! Say huzzah back. Please.

~ own_death
I have fallen. Nobly. Please remember it as noble.
Dead. A tragic scene. Very moving.
Slain! At least it was dramatic.
Death is just a plot twist.

~ other_death
{0} has fallen! A tragic turn!
Rise, {0}! Your tale isn't finished.
Rest, brave {0}. Briefly. Then get up.
Alas, {0}! Say alas back when you're up.

~ drop
{item}! A relic of legend! Probably.
{item}! It shall have a name.
Found {item}. My character treasures it already.
{item}! The quest provides.
